Version 1.9.2:
- Validate deferred counts in direct storage, omitted fields and built-in array
  padding before storage merging and object encoding, avoiding dropped storage
  and spurious 256-byte fills. Preserve valid zero-length fields and storage
  grouping in initialized and uninitialized structures.
- Retain labels reached through forward count aliases before unused-label
  removal, so listing and analysis options no longer change assembly results
  or unused-label warnings.
- Diagnose invalid dotted references and unresolved storage expressions without
  crashes or invalid objects, preserving existing output files on failure.
- Resolve forward constant aliases in ordinary operands and sizeof label data,
  with cycle detection and validation of the symbols at the end of a chain.
- Accept previously defined named counts in unions, in the constant scope,
  and avoid cascaded errors after an invalid union declaration.
- Cache completed integer aliases within each evaluation and remove repeated
  statement-list scans when expanding aggregates and merging adjacent data.
- Emit numeric .char data and relocations as bytes in objects. Preserve string
  character maps and match binary-mode out-of-range truncation warnings.
- Preserve listing schemas and instruction-record schema version 3. Deferred
  zero counts on omitted structure-array fields remain unsupported, and union
  dimensions must be known at declaration time. Other known limitations,
  including address-dependent counts and local-label aliases, remain in TODO.

Version 1.9.1:
- Validate deferred counts of explicitly initialized user-type array fields
  before storage merging and object encoding. Reject zero and negative counts,
  including counts defined after an instance, without replacing existing output.
- Resolve aliases and unary expressions in these counts, detect circular
  definitions, and preserve values already known when an instance is expanded.
- Remove zero padding before object encoding to avoid spurious 256-byte fills.
  Preserve adjacent storage grouping and listing source locations for previously
  correct inputs, including nested arrays and omitted subfields.
- Report field-specific errors for invalid named counts, matching literal-count
  diagnostics without cascading errors after an invalid initializer kind.
- Preserve listing schemas and instruction-record schema version 3. Other
  storage-count paths, ordinary-operand aliases and named union counts remain
  tracked in TODO, along with resolver and aggregate-instance performance work.

Version 1.9.0:
- Preserve the declared size of explicitly initialized user-type array fields
  in structures and unions: initialize the first element and zero-fill the rest.
  Improve invalid-count diagnostics and avoid cascaded padding errors.
- Continue assembly after empty initializer expansions and taken conditional
  branches, preserving following labels and data and avoiding assertion aborts
  after repeated initializer errors. Release unused structure fill expressions.
- Add opt-in --listing-version=2 for pure-binary JSON/NDJSON listings, with
  segment, byte-count and emission metadata, compressed storage fill, and
  emitting spans that partition the binary. Diagnostic listings do not claim
  bytes from a previous output file.
- Account for numeric .CHAR data in listing v2 and warn when an explicit
  listing version is supplied without a listing destination. Document offset
  joins and CPU-address wraparound.
- Preserve default listing v1 output and instruction-record schema version 3.
  Named and deferred user-type array count limitations remain tracked in TODO.

Version 1.8.2:
- Restore documented omitted fields in structure, union and record initializers.
  Leading, middle, trailing and consecutive omissions retain their positions
  and default to zero, including nested initializers and macro expansion.
- Correct padding for omitted user-defined fields and anonymous unions. Fix
  assertion aborts for .CHAR storage, omitted .CHAR fields and short strings.
- Diagnose unsupported gaps inside built-in array initializers explicitly.
- Add 16 regression tests covering emitted bytes, linked objects, character
  maps and label/listing/xref addresses after padding. Output schemas are unchanged.

Version 1.8.1:
- Correct structured-listing binary offsets after code-segment storage and
  non-emitting data-segment initialized data or .INCBIN. CPU addresses,
  assembled bytes and diagnostics are unchanged.
- Add 28 regression subcases covering storage widths, empty storage records,
  segment switches and continuations in JSON/NDJSON and debug/non-debug modes.
- Keep listing schema version 1 and instruction-record schema version 3.
  Non-emitting data-segment rows still lack per-row emission metadata; see TODO.

Version 1.8.0:
- Incompatible analysis-format change: instruction records now use schema
  version 3, with a shared files table and integer file indices in every span.
  Older records schemas are no longer emitted; consumers must update.
- Add explicit memory-access facts and signed additive operand terms with
  per-use symbol bindings, including reassigned constants.
- Correct access classification across cross-references and analyses: model
  read-modify-write sites as both reads and writes, BIT/CMP as reads, pointer
  operands as pointer reads, and immediate operands as immediate references.
  See XASM_INSTRUCTION_RECORDS_V2_SPEC.md for the complete migration contract.
- Reduce instruction-record size and serialization cost through shared paths,
  faster span output, and buffering of the standalone records file. Add a
  default performance-regression limit to the real-project comparison tool.
- Install generated xasm/xlnk man pages and a worked analysis-feature guide;
  include them in the tested source distribution.

Version 1.7.0:
- Add FCEUX ROM/RAM debugger name export using physical PRG page offsets,
  independent of xref filters, with optional 16 KiB NROM mirroring.
- Add versioned instruction/operand records, standalone instruction sidecars,
  data-directive references, and content-hashed dependency manifests.
- Add structured listings, xref summaries, data-reference and index-pattern
  analyses, data consumers/coverage, raw-address audits, and binary comparison.
- Preserve output destinations on failed sidecar writes, closes, and renames;
  report listing and stdout analysis errors.
- Improve parser, AST removal, symbol lookup, and JSON serialization costs.
- Check linker writes and closes, preserving existing files on failure, including
  scripts that switch output destinations.
- Grow symbol scope storage safely and reject failed symbol-name allocations.
- Reject malformed/truncated object files and malformed linker scripts; clean up
  incomplete parses and test allocation failures and excessive nesting.
- Include tests and feature specifications in source archives. Test unpacked
  archives and installed tools on Linux/macOS, with sanitizer checks on Linux.

Version 1.6.1:
- Modernize autotools
Version 1.6.0:
- Added support for .w ("wide") mnemonic suffix to force 16-bit address encoding. This can
  be used to disable the default zero page optimization of instructions. Example:
  lda.w $006B
Version 1.5.2:
- Fixed a bunch of issues
Version 1.5.0:
- Added some stuff, fixed some bugs
Version 1.4.5:
- xasm: fixed bug that prevented local labels from being used as operand to DB, DW, DD directives
- xasm: fixed bug in processing of array of operands to DB, DW, DD directives
- xasm: negative immediate operand no longer gives truncated warning as long as it fits in signed byte (DB) or word (DW) 
- xasm: added BLT, BGE as aliases for BCC, BCS
- xlnk: prints physical addresses of relocated public symbols when --verbose
Version 1.4.4:
- xlnk: fixed bug in RAM allocator
- xlnk: prints statistics on RAM management (total, used, left) when --verbose
Version 1.4.3:
- xasm: support for anonymous unions
- xasm: fixed bug in result of sizeof operator when applied to an initialized structure variable
- xasm, xlnk: returns error code so that i.e. Make stops after the first erroneous invocation
Version 1.4.2:
- xasm: symbols can be indexed statically
- xasm: sizeof operator now works correctly when applied to an array
- xasm: fixed bug that lead to dysfunctional symbol table when using `=' equates
- xlnk: fixed bug in RAM allocator
- xlnk: fixed line number bug in error messages
- xlnk: removed duplicate error message (unresolved symbols)
Version 1.4.1:
- xasm: Fixed bug in processing of declaration of array of user-defined type
- xasm: Fixed bug that lead to no error message when declaring an uninitialized variable of non-existing user-defined type
- xlnk: Fixed imperfection in allocation of alignment-constrained data
- xlnk: Fixed memory leak in RAM allocator
Version 1.4.0:
- xasm: added --debug switch, which retains file locations in the object file
- xasm: LABEL directive can take specific address as argument
- xasm: constraints can be communicated to linker on how contents of data segments should be mapped to RAM
- xasm: PUBLIC modifier can be specified directly when defining a variable
- xasm: fixed bug in code generation of exported string constants
- xlnk: prints the filename and location of the source of a link-time error (if unit assembled with --debug switch)
- xlnk: rewrote data segment mapping function to take zeropage and alignment constraints into account
- xlnk: improved code relocation
- xlnk: fixed linker script parsing bug
Version 1.3.5:
- xasm: added ability to declare storage for array of user-defined types, C-style (works for native types too)
- xasm: added ability to specify the type of data that a label addresses
- xasm: fixed bug in code generation of storage of user-defined types
- xasm: fixed some error detection and parsing woes
- xasm: added DEFINE directive (same semantics as EQU, but potentially more compact)
- xlnk: fixed code relocation bug
- xlnk: implemented bank operator (^)
- xlnk: --verbose switch now gives helpful info on what the linker is doing
Version 1.3.0:
- xasm: added support for user-defined records (RECORD directive, MASK operator)
- xasm: added WHILE directive
- xasm: implemented ELIF directive
- xasm: improved --define switch: value can now be given (i.e. --define a=10)
- xasm: SIZEOF operator now works on variable identifiers too
- xasm: fixed bug that prevented single-character identifiers from working
- xasm: added --no-warn switch to suppress warnings
- xasm: early support for --verbose switch
Version 1.2.0:
- xasm: support for forward/backward branches
- xasm: fixed bug that caused INCSRC to run out of file handles
- xasm: fixed erroneous parsing of lines with < > operators
Version 1.1.0:
- xasm: support for structs, unions and enums
- xasm: support for anonymous macros (REPT)
- xasm: new directives: PROC, LABEL, PAD, MESSAGE
- xasm: syntactic improvements
- xasm: important bug fixes for IF/ELSE and INCBIN
- xasm: added switch: --swap-parens
- xasm: improved literal expression folding
- xasm: preliminary support for --define=IDENT switch
Version 1.0.2:
- xasm, xlnk: not using argp for argument parsing anymore; increased portability
- xasm: removed X86-dependent timing code
Version 1.0.1:
- xlnk: fixed bug in code relocation
- xlnk: fixed bug in 'pad' script command execution
- xasm: fixed bug that made xasm crash when expanding a macro with no arguments
- xasm: fixed bug in error location output (sometimes filename would be "(null)")
- updated documentation

